# Shell scripts run on Linux boxes but are edited on Windows. A CRLF shebang
# line ("/usr/bin/env bash\r") makes the kernel look for an interpreter whose
# name ends in a carriage return, and the box reports "bad interpreter: no such
# file or directory" while pointing at a file that plainly exists. Pin LF
# regardless of the local core.autocrlf setting.
*.sh text eol=lf
